window.docContents[65].resolve({"/Hoare2/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare2___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-II--Formal-Decorated-Programs--More-Automation":{"contents":"The propositions generated by DCom.VerificationConditions are fairly\nbig and contain many conjuncts that are essentially trivial.\n\nexample : decWhile.VerificationConditions := by\n  rw [Decorated.VerificationConditions, decWhile]\n  simp only [DCom.VerificationConditions,\n    DCom.postcondition]\n  sorry\n\n\n\n\nFortunately, our verify_assertion tactic can generally take care of\nmost (or sometimes all) of them.\n\nexample : decWhile.VerificationConditions := by\n  simp only [decWhile]\n  verify_assertion\n\n\n\n\nTo automate the overall process of verification, we can use\nverification_conditions_correct to extract the verification conditions, use\nverify_assertion to verify them as much as it can, and finally tidy\nup any remaining bits by hand.\n\nmacro \"verify\" : tactic =>\n  `(tactic|\n    (apply verification_conditions_correct;\n     verify_assertion))\n\n\n\n\nHere's the final, formal proof that decWhile is correct.\n\ntheorem dec_while_correct : decWhile.OuterTripleValid := by\n  simp only [decWhile]\n  verify\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Hoare Logic\u0009Hoare2: Hoare Logic, Part II\u0009Formal Decorated Programs","header":"6.2.3. More Automation","id":"/Hoare2/#Hoare-Logic--Hoare2___-Hoare-Logic___-Part-II--Formal-Decorated-Programs--More-Automation"}});